---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import RecordLookupTool from '../components/RecordLookupTool.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="A Record Lookup" description="A record lookup for any domain: see the IPv4 addresses it points to, with TTLs, live via DNS-over-HTTPS.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/tools/" class="hover:text-accent">Tools</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">A Record Lookup</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">A Record Lookup</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-dim">The A record maps a hostname to its IPv4 address. Check yours to confirm where a domain points before and after migrations.</p>
    <div class="mt-8"><RecordLookupTool type="A" label="A Record Lookup" hint="Lookups run in your browser via public DNS-over-HTTPS. Nothing is logged." /></div>
    <article class="rich-text mt-12 max-w-none">
      <h2>How to read the results</h2>
      <p>An A record answer is an IPv4 address belonging to the server or CDN edge that serves the domain. Multiple answers mean round-robin distribution: traffic splits across the listed addresses, with no health checking, so a dead server keeps its share until the record is edited.</p>
      <p>The TTL column shows how long resolvers may cache each answer. High TTLs mean edits take hours to appear everywhere; low TTLs mean minutes. Compare values after any change to confirm the cutover landed.</p>
      <div class="grid gap-2"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-4 py-3 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="cursor-pointer list-none font-medium text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Why does the IP differ from my hosting panel?<span class="float-right text-accent">+</span></summary><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">A cached answer whose TTL has not expired, or a proxied CDN setup that intentionally hides the origin. Both are normal.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-4 py-3 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="cursor-pointer list-none font-medium text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can one A record point at several IPs?<span class="float-right text-accent">+</span></summary><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes, that is round-robin distribution: it spreads load but does not remove dead servers from rotation.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-4 py-3 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="cursor-pointer list-none font-medium text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">A record vs CNAME for www?<span class="float-right text-accent">+</span></summary><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">A points www at an IP directly; CNAME aliases it. Never both on the same name.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-4 py-3 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="cursor-pointer list-none font-medium text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How do I change my A record without downtime?<span class="float-right text-accent">+</span></summary><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Lower TTL to 300 a day ahead, keep the old server live through the window, change the record, verify propagation, then decommission.</p></details></div>
      
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How do I verify my changes?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Run the record lookup to confirm live values, then check the propagation checker for worldwide agreement. Both tools run in your browser.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What TTL should I use?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">3600 seconds is the default. Drop to 300 a day before changes so cutover is quick, then restore.</p></details></div>
<h2>Related</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/a-record/">A records explained (guide)</a></li>
        <li><a href="/dns-record-lookup/">All-in-one record lookup</a> and <a href="/dns-propagation-checker/">propagation checker</a></li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
